// Destination facts ported from the Swedish sibling project flyg.ai
// (data/destinations.ts, 2.7 MB). Flyamba's own catalog was ported from the same
// source but kept only slug/name/country/continent/prices/images — the editorial
// scores, tags, cost-of-living figures and local content were dropped, which is
// why AI search had nothing to match "beach" on and result cards looked empty
// next to the 8 hand-authored destinations.
//
// WHAT WAS PORTED:
//   scores        1–10 editorial ratings, all 550 destinations
//   tags          normalized to a controlled English vocabulary
//   foodPerDay    food & drink per day, converted SEK → USD
//   hotelPerNight mid-range hotel per night, converted SEK → USD
//   dishes        local dish NAMES, 309 destinations
//   sights        top sight NAMES, 309 destinations
//
// DISHES AND SIGHTS ARE NAMES ONLY. flyg.ai stores them as
// "Bullit de peix — ibizenisk fiskgryta längs nordkusten": a proper noun, an
// em-dash, then a Swedish description. Only the part before the dash is kept,
// which is language-neutral and needs no translation. Entries whose name half
// still contains Swedish ("Diocletianus palats", "Cofete strand", "Oia
// solnedgången") are dropped rather than shipped half-translated — about 31% of
// them. Recovering those needs a real translation pass, not a bigger regex.
//
// TAGS are a controlled vocabulary, not a translation. flyg.ai had 283 distinct
// Swedish tags with a long tail of place names ("Mallorca", "Zanzibar") that
// duplicate the country field, plus Swedish-market-only tags ("Inrikes",
// "Sverige", "Direktflyg" — which meant direct *from Stockholm* and is simply
// false here). Those were dropped; the rest collapse onto the vocabulary below.
//
// `tagsDerived: true` marks the 237 destinations whose tags were inferred from
// their own scores (axis >= 8) because flyg.ai had none for them. Without this
// the tagged minority dominated results: a beach search returned Benidorm and
// Sitges — tagged — over Fuerteventura (beaches 10) and Rhodes (9), which were
// not. Treat derived tags as weaker evidence than authored ones.
//
// SCORES: flyg.ai's sixth axis is `culture`; Flyamba's schema calls the same
// axis `activities`. Mapped on the way in. The scores are editorial judgements
// authored for a Swedish audience — `value` in particular is relative to Swedish
// prices, and some are plainly wrong (Tirana, 35 km inland, scores 7 on beaches).
//
// NOT PORTED: `insiderTip` (all 552 exist but are full Swedish sentences) and
// the long-form SEO prose. Those need an actual translation pass.
//
// PRICES ELSEWHERE IN THE CATALOG remain Stockholm-origin fares in SEK. That is
// inherited from flyg.ai and is NOT fixed by this file.
//
// SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Do not import this from a "use client" file — it is ~110 kB
// and would ship to the browser. /api/ai-search reads it and sends only what a
// card needs; the compare page needs a server-component refactor before it can.

export type DestinationScores = {
  beaches: number;
  nightlife: number;
  food: number;
  activities: number;
  family: number;
  value: number;
};

export type DestinationFacts = {
  scores: DestinationScores;
  /** Controlled vocabulary — see TAG_VOCABULARY. */
  tags?: string[];
  /** True when `tags` were inferred from scores rather than authored. */
  tagsDerived?: boolean;
  /** Food & drink per day, USD, e.g. "$33–48". */
  foodPerDay?: string;
  /** Mid-range hotel per night, USD, e.g. "$95–133". */
  hotelPerNight?: string;
  /** Local dish names, up to 3. */
  dishes?: string[];
  /** Top sight names, up to 3. */
  sights?: string[];
  /** One-sentence local tip, translated from flyg.ai's Swedish original.
   *  Populated by scripts/translate-facts.mjs — empty until that has run. */
  insiderTip?: string;
};

